{
  "requirement": "An ask builder begins in `ContextPhase`. Only that state exposes `context`,\ncomposing the reusable prefix under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.agent_context`. The first\ncall to `contents_of_current_node`, `contents_of_node`, or `contents_of_successors` enters `NodePhase`, even\nwith an empty successor selection. This state allows further node insertions\nand awaiting, with no `context` method or transition back. The builder's types\nenforce the restriction.",
  "determination": false,
  "rationale": "Add a test, for example by extending `task_messages_share_a_prefix_and_can_queue_another_node` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs`, that calls `contents_of_node` on an `Ask` that is already in `NodePhase`. For example, it could chain `.contents_of_current_node().contents_of_node(selected)`. It should assert that the node contents are sent in insertion order and that the dependencies are recorded. Mark it with `{test}` for `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.judge.phases`. — `judge.phases` says `NodePhase` allows further node insertions. The runtime tests exercise this only for `contents_of_current_node` and `contents_of_successors` in `explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots`. In `task_messages_share_a_prefix_and_can_queue_another_node`, `contents_of_node` is called only once, from `ContextPhase`, despite the test name. An implementation that offered `contents_of_node` only on `ContextPhase` would pass every reviewed test. That would violate the requirement for one of the three insertion methods.",
